The mayor shall have the following duties:
(1) Presiding at meetings. To preside at all meetings of the city council, but the mayor shall not be allowed to vote at such meetings.
(2) Appointment of officers and employees. To appoint with the advice and consent of the city council all officers and employees of the city whose election or appointment is not otherwise provided for.
(3) Dismissal, suspension, and discipline of officers and employees for cause. To dismiss with the advice and consent of council, suspend, or discipline for cause all officers and employees under the mayor's control provided that for the purposes of this section "cause" shall include, but not be limited to:
a. Discrimination;
b. Harassment;
c. Sexual harassment;
d. Substance abuse;
e. Acts of workplace violence;
f. Inappropriate appearance;
g. Ethics violations;
h. Negligence or inefficiency in performing the duties of the position held;
i. Unfitness to perform assigned duties;
j. Misconduct;
k. Insubordination;
l. Conduct reflecting discredit on the city;
m. Failure to report for work without justifiable cause;
n. Chronic absenteeism; tardiness;
o. Political activity in violation of municipal regulations;
p. Breach of confidentiality.
(4) Dismissal of officers and employees without cause. All employees of the city shall be employees at will, and the city or the employee may also terminate the employment relationship at any time, with or without prior notice, warning, procedure or formality, for any reason or no reason, with the only obligation being the payment of wages earned.
(5) Preparation of annual report. To prepare and present to the council an annual report of the city's affairs.
(6) Executing legal documents. To sign and execute all contracts, deeds, and bonds of the city duly authorized by the mayor and council
(Ord. No. O-45-07, § 3-302, 4-19-2007)
State Law reference— Authority of municipality to establish, define, and regulate duties and powers of municipal officers, O.C.G.A. § 36-34-2.

